---
description: After every merge or PR close, delete the head branch the same session.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Delete merged branches

Hard rule. Do not wait for the user to ask.

After a pull request is merged or closed, finish delivery in the same session:

1. Prefer `gh pr merge --delete-branch`.
2. If origin still has the head: `git push origin --delete <head-branch>`.
3. Delete the local head (`git branch -d` / `-D` if already merged).
4. `git fetch origin --prune`.
5. Confirm the head is gone. A merged PR whose branch is still on origin is unfinished.

Never delete `main`. Never delete a branch that still has an open PR.
